  "md": "# Benchmark report\n\nRun: <DIR>  \nSuite: lite, model claude-sonnet-5.5, effort high, 1 task(s), kiro-cli kiro-cli 2.35.1  \nBaseline: vanilla. Judges: none (run the judge command for rubric and pairwise results)\n\nHow to read: efficiency cells (credits, calls, wall clock, tokens) are `median [95% bootstrap CI of the median]` over clean passes only, meaning status success, no infrastructure error, no model mismatch and every deterministic check passed. Failed runs never enter a median, so they cannot make an arm look cheap; they are shown as rates beside every cost figure (timeout, error, infra, model mismatch, checks failed, budget-skipped). \"success\" is the share of runs that finished cleanly; \"pass\" also needs every check to pass. \"credits per successful run\" is the total charged over all executed runs divided by clean passes, so failures raise it; a run killed before its final metering event is charged the runner's ledger value, not its partial figure. Tokens are not exposed by kiro-cli, so credits are the cost measure and estTokens is transcript characters / 4, an estimate. \"asked user\" is the share of runs whose final message ended with a question or an approval request. Win/tie/loss counts pairwise verdicts of the arm against the baseline, pooled over judges.\n\n## Flags\n\nNone.\n\n## Results\n\n### overall\n| arm | n | ok/timeout/error | success | pass | asked user | rubric score, scored (raw judge verdicts) | win/tie/loss vs vanilla | credits per successful run |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| vanilla | 3 | 3/0/0 | 100% | 100% | n/a | n/a | - | 3.00<br>timeout 0%; error 0%, infra 0%, model mismatch 0%, checks failed 0% |\n| v1.2.0 | 3 | 3/0/0 | 100% | 100% | n/a | n/a | - | 5.00<br>timeout 0%; error 0%, infra 0%, model mismatch 0%, checks failed 0% |\n\n| arm | clean passes in medians | credits | modelCalls | toolCalls | subagentCalls | wallClock s | estTokens (estimate) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| vanilla | 3 of 3 | 3.00 [2.00, 4.00]<br>timeout 0%; error 0%, infra 0%, model mismatch 0%, checks failed 0% | 2.0 [2.0, 2.0] | 3.0 [3.0, 3.0] | 0.0 [0.0, 0.0] | 1.0 [1.0, 1.0] | 100 [100, 100] |\n| v1.2.0 | 3 of 3 | 5.00 [4.00, 6.00]<br>timeout 0%; error 0%, infra 0%, model mismatch 0%, checks failed 0% | 2.0 [2.0, 2.0] | 3.0 [3.0, 3.0] | 0.0 [0.0, 0.0] | 1.0 [1.0, 1.0] | 100 [100, 100] |\n\n### simple\n| arm | n | ok/timeout/error | success | pass | asked user | rubric score, scored (raw judge verdicts) | win/tie/loss vs vanilla | credits per successful run |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| vanilla | 3 | 3/0/0 | 100% | 100% | n/a | n/a | - | 3.00<br>timeout 0%; error 0%, infra 0%, model mismatch 0%, checks failed 0% |\n| v1.2.0 | 3 | 3/0/0 | 100% | 100% | n/a | n/a | - | 5.00<br>timeout 0%; error 0%, infra 0%, model mismatch 0%, checks failed 0% |\n\n| arm | clean passes in medians | credits | modelCalls | toolCalls | subagentCalls | wallClock s | estTokens (estimate) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| vanilla | 3 of 3 | 3.00 [2.00, 4.00]<br>timeout 0%; error 0%, infra 0%, model mismatch 0%, checks failed 0% | 2.0 [2.0, 2.0] | 3.0 [3.0, 3.0] | 0.0 [0.0, 0.0] | 1.0 [1.0, 1.0] | 100 [100, 100] |\n| v1.2.0 | 3 of 3 | 5.00 [4.00, 6.00]<br>timeout 0%; error 0%, infra 0%, model mismatch 0%, checks failed 0% | 2.0 [2.0, 2.0] | 3.0 [3.0, 3.0] | 0.0 [0.0, 0.0] | 1.0 [1.0, 1.0] | 100 [100, 100] |\n"
